# Next.js App Router conventions

Full reference: `.cursor/PROJECT-OVERVIEW.md`

This project uses **App Router only** — one route at `/`.

## Layout (`src/app/layout.tsx`)

- Server component
- Loads global styles, Geist fonts
- `suppressHydrationWarning` on `<html>` and `<body>` (browser extensions inject attributes)
- Wraps children in `AppProviders`

## Page (`src/app/page.tsx`)

Thin wrapper only:

```tsx
import { WorkforceActivity } from 'src/modules/WorkforceActivity';

export default function HomePage(): React.ReactElement {
  return <WorkforceActivity />;
}
```

## Providers (`src/app/providers.tsx`)

Client component:

```txt
AppThemeProvider → ActivityProvider → children
```

## Rules

- Pages do not contain business logic or feature UI sections
- View switching happens inside `WorkforceActivity` module via context
- Mark client boundaries with `'use client'` where hooks/context are used

## Do NOT

- Add Pages Router routes
- Use `getLayout` pattern
- Fetch from APIs in `app/` files
